# Kramak (क्रमक) — Cursor Rules
# Universal Base: .kramak/AGENTS.md | .kramak/SKILL.md

When triggered ("Start", "begin", "continue", "go"):
1. Read `.kramak/state.json` (if missing, initialize with `phase: "bootstrap"`).
2. Read `.kramak/ROUTER.md` for non-negotiable invariants and phase routing.

## .mdc Progressive Loading Rules
- **Rule 1 (Always Active):** Load `.kramak/ROUTER.md` on all interactions. Enforce Grounded Verification, 3-Tier Scope Check, and Circuit Breaker invariants.
- **Rule 2 (Planning / Bootstrap / Dispatch Mode):** When `state.phase == "bootstrap" | "planning" | "dispatch"` or editing `.kramak/work-items/**`, load `.kramak/planner/CORE.md`.
- **Rule 3 (Execution / Merge Queue Mode):** When `state.phase == "executing" | "merge_queue"` or editing source files targeted by active Work Item, load `.kramak/executor/CORE.md`.
- **Rule 4 (Auditing Mode):** When `state.phase == "auditing"`, load `.kramak/executor/CORE.md` (§AUDIT).
- **Rule 5 (Resume / Recovery Mode):** When `state.phase == "waiting" | "escalated" | "complete"`, load `.kramak/planner/CORE.md` (§RESUME).

## Execution Constraints
- Verify all code references against live files before making changes.
- Run test/build suites after each code edit.
- Update `.kramak/state.json` atomically on every Work Item state transition.
